        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4b0d1149-c262-513b-841c-e4e0bc04309b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yamaji Motoharu\n- Organizations: Imperial Japanese Army, Japanese Second Army, First Division\n- Places: Port Arthur, Lüshunkou, Empire of Japan\n- Events: First Sino-Japanese War, Port Arthur massacre\n\nFacts:\n- Yamaji Motoharu was born on 10 September 1841 and died on 3 October 1897.\n- The Imperial Japanese Army was the official ground-based armed force of the Empire of Japan from 1868 to 1945.\n- Yamaji Motoharu was a Japanese general in the early Imperial Japanese Army.\n- During the First Sino-Japanese War, the Port Arthur massacre occurred from 21 November 1894 for two or three days in the Chinese coastal city of Port Arthur, now Lüshunkou.\n- Advanced elements of the First Division of the Japanese Second Army were under the command of General Yamaji Motoharu during the Port Arthur massacre.\n- During the Port Arthur massacre, those Japanese forces killed somewhere between 1,000 and 20,000 Chinese servicemen and civilians.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
